---
// Timeoff — JPL Redesign case study. STRIPPED: the painterly /work backdrop kept as-is,
// NO mat — a single plain left-hung column sits straight on the painting. Red is a whisper
// (kicker/title), warm-ink body, everything shares one left edge (ref: Studio Small).
// Pacing is ONE BEAT PER SCREEN, each block rising into frame on scroll. Media = 1060px. Inter.
import { Picture, Image } from 'astro:assets';
import studio from '../assets/jpl-studio.jpg';
import about from '../assets/jpl-about.png';
import inspoRoom from '../assets/inspo-room.png';
import inspoStudioSmall from '../assets/inspo-studiosmall.png';
import inspoMahdavi from '../assets/inspo-mahdavi.png';
import inspoAshby from '../assets/inspo-ashby.png';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>JPL Redesign — Timeoff</title>
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400..800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
    <script is:inline>
      // Paint the mobile theme from the first frame: stamp <html> before <body> renders,
      // so there's no flash of the desktop (red text / textured bg) on navigation.
      if (window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(max-width: 768px)').matches) {
        document.documentElement.classList.add('is-mobile');
      }
    </script>
    <script is:inline>
      if (sessionStorage.getItem('navTL')) {
        document.documentElement.classList.add('pre-tl');
        sessionStorage.removeItem('navTL');
      }
    </script>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="page">
      <!-- ——— hero ——— -->
      <section class="panel hero-panel">
        <header class="hero">
          <p class="kicker reveal">Web Design · Front End · 2026</p>
          <h1 class="title reveal">Jesse Parris-Lamb</h1>
          <p class="subtitle reveal">Website Redesign – Unofficial</p>
          <p class="scroll-hint reveal">Scroll ↓</p>
        </header>
      </section>

      <!-- ——— intro: studio photo, then the story ——— -->
      <section class="panel">
        <figure class="media reveal">
          <Picture
            src={studio}
            formats={['avif', 'webp']}
            alt="Inside the Jesse Parris-Lamb studio — a walnut worktable with cane chairs against shelves of archive boxes and design books"
            widths={[768, 1280, 1600, 2000]}
            sizes="(max-width: 880px) 86vw, 860px"
            loading="eager"
          />
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="panel text-panel">
        <div class="text reveal">
          <p class="lead">I recently moved to Brooklyn and have started to spend a few hours a day at the Brooklyn Public Library near Prospect Park to get some work done. I&rsquo;ve been looking for inspiration for my next project, and on my first day walking to the library in the morning, I walk past this interesting &ldquo;storefront&rdquo; that looked different from the rest on the street.</p>
          <p>I did a quick look on Apple Maps and saw it was the home of Jesse Parris-Lamb: a Brooklyn-based interior design firm founded in 2014 &mdash; and they do really cool work. When I got to the library, I checked out their website and thought &ldquo;I can probably do better&rdquo; (humbly, of course) so here we are&hellip;</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ——— the home page ——— -->
      <section class="panel">
        <figure class="media reveal">
          <p class="caption">The home page..</p>
          <div class="vimeo-wrapper">
            <iframe loading="lazy" src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/1201950009?autopause=0&muted=1&controls=0&loop=1&title=0&byline=0&portrait=0" frameborder="0" allow="autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen></iframe>
          </div>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="panel text-panel">
        <div class="text reveal">
          <p>I wanted to try and capture the essence of JPL&rsquo;s design in this website. To me, they show a lot of expression, but a lot of restraint. They add a lot of character to spaces, a lot of flair&hellip; but it all seems very familiar and not overdone. That&rsquo;s tough to nail. So the website reflects the same principles: charming and familiar at face value, but very unique and intentional. Everything has to have a purpose.</p>
          <p>The goal of the home page was to get straight to the point. Get you into the world of Jesse Parris-Lamb as soon as you land on the website. I think the home page is a great execution of user guidance as well &mdash; tough to put into words, but I don&rsquo;t feel overwhelmed on the home page. I have everything I would want.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ——— interior gallery ——— -->
      <section class="panel">
        <figure class="media reveal">
          <p class="caption">The interior gallery..</p>
          <div class="vimeo-wrapper">
            <iframe loading="lazy" src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/1201950010?autopause=0&muted=1&controls=0&loop=1&title=0&byline=0&portrait=0" frameborder="0" allow="autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen></iframe>
          </div>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="panel text-panel">
        <p class="reveal">Interior gallery was an area I had to show a lot of restraint. Something bold or super &ldquo;experience&rdquo; heavy didn&rsquo;t fit into the vibe I had assigned to this project. A few nice touches went a long way here: a subtle parallax scroll and some hover effects to give the thumbnails some life.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- ——— space gallery ——— -->
      <section class="panel">
        <figure class="media reveal">
          <p class="caption">A space gallery..</p>
          <div class="vimeo-wrapper">
            <iframe loading="lazy" src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/1201950562?autopause=0&muted=1&controls=0&loop=1&title=0&byline=0&portrait=0" frameborder="0" allow="autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen></iframe>
          </div>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="panel text-panel">
        <p class="reveal">The gallery for each space was based off of reference images I generated for inspiration. I like how the large, off-center images sort of command a lot of space and attention, yet the write-up to the left seems to have the same amount of pull. Idk, it was a fun use of spacing. The film strip on the bottom is a nice touch as well &mdash; the page felt incomplete and cheap without it.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- ——— about page ——— -->
      <section class="panel">
        <figure class="media reveal">
          <p class="caption">The about page..</p>
          <Picture
            src={about}
            formats={['avif', 'webp']}
            alt="The Jesse Parris-Lamb About page — a black-and-white monogram sculpture beside a portrait of the firm's founders"
            widths={[768, 1280, 1600, 2000]}
            sizes="(max-width: 880px) 86vw, 860px"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="panel text-panel">
        <div class="text reveal">
          <p>Finally, the about page &mdash; which unironically is my favorite page of the project. I kept getting stuck trying to turn the about page into a whole experience, and it just never felt right. The original about page on JPL&rsquo;s site is very simple and plain, but that&rsquo;s why it&rsquo;s good. I came to the conclusion that the rest of the site is designed to be an experience for their work&hellip; the about page should not be competing with that. I want to see the story, and I want to see it quickly and all at once.</p>
          <p>I pulled inspiration from a website I had in my references that made really good use of full-bleed images and color contrast. The other pages I had built were pretty uniform, so I felt that the about page was fair game for a slight departure in design. It feels special, but still not overdone.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ——— original site ——— -->
      <section class="panel">
        <figure class="media reveal">
          <p class="caption">The original site..</p>
          <div class="vimeo-wrapper">
            <iframe loading="lazy" src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/1201951169?autopause=0&muted=1&controls=0&loop=1&title=0&byline=0&portrait=0" frameborder="0" allow="autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen></iframe>
          </div>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="panel text-panel">
        <p class="reveal">Here is the original (current) website. It&rsquo;s fine, but it doesn&rsquo;t feel special. To me, it didn&rsquo;t reflect the level of work that Jesse Parris-Lamb does.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- ——— closing: reference deck + visit the live site ——— -->
      <section class="panel closing-panel">
        <div class="closing">
          <p class="caption reveal">A few of my references..</p>
          <div class="closing-row reveal">
            <div class="stack">
              <div class="stack-card stack-card-1"><Image src={inspoRoom} alt="Reference: a minimalist living room with a website on the screen" widths={[480, 960]} sizes="460px" loading="lazy" /></div>
              <div class="stack-card stack-card-2"><Image src={inspoStudioSmall} alt="Reference: StudioSmall website" widths={[480, 960]} sizes="460px" loading="lazy" /></div>
              <div class="stack-card stack-card-3"><Image src={inspoMahdavi} alt="Reference: India Mahdavi website" widths={[480, 960]} sizes="460px" loading="lazy" /></div>
              <div class="stack-card stack-card-4"><Image src={inspoAshby} alt="Reference: Studio Ashby website" widths={[480, 960]} sizes="460px" loading="lazy" /></div>
            </div>
            <div class="visit-block">
              <img class="visit-note" src="/click_to_visit_trim.png" alt="Click to visit the site" width="340" height="64" />
              <a class="omnibox" href="https://jpl-redesign.vercel.app/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the live JPL redesign at jpl-redesign.vercel.app">
                <svg class="omnibox-lock" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor"><path d="M11 7V5a3 3 0 0 0-6 0v2H4v7h8V7h-1zm-4-2a1 1 0 0 1 2 0v2H7V5z"/></svg>
                <span class="omnibox-url">jpl-redesign.vercel.app</span>
                <svg class="omnibox-arrow" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg>
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ——— next project ——— -->
      <section class="panel next-panel">
        <a class="next reveal" href="/bird-dog">
          <span class="next-kicker">Next</span>
          <span class="next-title">Bird Dog</span>
        </a>
      </section>
    </main>

    <nav class="chrome" aria-label="site">
      <a class="label tl work grow" href="/work">Work</a>
      <a class="label tr info grow" href="/information">Information</a>
    </nav>

    <style>
      :root {
        --fg: #d6352a;                       /* red — accent (kicker, title) */
        --ink: #26241f;                      /* warm near-black — body reading ink */
        --muted: rgba(38, 36, 31, 0.5);      /* captions */
      }
      * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
      html { background: #eef0ec; scroll-behavior: smooth; }
      body {
        /* painterly backdrop, kept as-is — content sits straight on the painting, no mat */
        background: #eef0ec url('/work-bg.png') center / cover no-repeat fixed;
        color: var(--ink);
        font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
        -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
        min-height: 100vh;
      }

      /* ——— the column: one plain centered measure; painting shows in the gutters ——— */
      .page {
        position: relative;
        z-index: 1;
        max-width: min(92vw, 1080px);
        margin: 0 auto;
        /* content fades in on load; .leaving dips it before we navigate away */
        animation: page-in 0.55s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1) backwards;
        transition: opacity 0.3s ease-out;
      }
      @keyframes page-in {
        from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(10px); }
        to   { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
      }
      .page.leaving { opacity: 0; }
      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        .page { animation: none; }
        .page.leaving { opacity: 1; transition: none; }
      }

      /* ——— one beat per screen, everything hung to the same left edge ——— */
      .panel {
        min-height: 100vh;
        display: grid;
        align-content: center;
        justify-items: start;
        padding: 12vh 0;
      }

      /* ——— hero ——— */
      .hero { text-align: left; }
      .kicker { font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--fg); margin-bottom: 1.4rem; }
      .title { font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 7vw, 5.4rem); font-weight: 400; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -0.012em; color: var(--fg); }
      .subtitle { font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 7vw, 5.4rem); font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.04; letter-spacing: -0.012em; color: var(--fg); margin-top: 0.2rem; }
      .scroll-hint { font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 3.5rem; }

      /* ——— bare media — no frame, no shadow, demos/screengrabs all at 1060px ——— */
      .media { max-width: 1060px; width: 100%; }
      .caption { font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--muted); letter-spacing: 0.01em; margin-bottom: 0.7rem; }
      .media :global(img), .media .vimeo-wrapper { display: block; }
      .media :global(img) { width: 100%; height: auto; }
      .vimeo-wrapper { position: relative; width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 416 / 240; overflow: hidden; background: #ddd; }
      .vimeo-wrapper iframe { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: none; }

      /* ——— text: quiet, left-hung, one calm treatment (ref: Studio Small) ——— */
      .text-panel p {
        max-width: 58ch;
        font-size: clamp(1.02rem, 1.35vw, 1.16rem);
        font-weight: 400;
        line-height: 1.7;
        color: var(--ink);
      }
      .text { max-width: 58ch; }
      .text p { max-width: none; }
      .text p + p { margin-top: 1.4rem; }

      /* ——— reveal-on-scroll: rises into frame, weighted easing ——— */
      .reveal {
        opacity: 0;
        transform: translateY(40px);
        transition: opacity 1s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1), transform 1s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
        will-change: opacity, transform;
      }
      .reveal.in { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        .reveal { opacity: 1 !important; transform: none !important; transition: none; }
      }

      /* ——— closing reference deck ——— */
      .closing-panel { min-height: 100vh; }
      .closing { width: 100%; max-width: 980px; }
      .closing-row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 3.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
      .stack { position: relative; flex: 0 0 auto; width: clamp(280px, 38vw, 460px); aspect-ratio: 3 / 2; }
      .stack-card { position: absolute; top: 50%; left: 50%; width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 3 / 2; border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden; background: #fff; box-shadow: 0 14px 34px rgba(0,0,0,0.2); will-change: transform, opacity; }
      .stack-card :global(img) { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; display: block; }
      .stack-card-1 { z-index: 1; transform: translate(-50%, -50%) translate(-16px, 14px) rotate(-7deg); }
      .stack-card-2 { z-index: 2; transform: translate(-50%, -50%) translate(12px, 8px) rotate(5deg); animation: stack2 2.6s linear infinite alternate; }
      .stack-card-3 { z-index: 3; transform: translate(-50%, -50%) translate(-6px, 0) rotate(-3deg); animation: stack3 2.6s linear infinite alternate; }
      .stack-card-4 { z-index: 4; transform: translate(-50%, -50%) translate(8px, -8px) rotate(2deg); animation: stack4 2.6s linear infinite alternate; }
      @keyframes stack2 { 0%, 8% { opacity: 0; } 9%, 100% { opacity: 1; } }
      @keyframes stack3 { 0%, 38% { opacity: 0; } 39%, 100% { opacity: 1; } }
      @keyframes stack4 { 0%, 68% { opacity: 0; } 69%, 100% { opacity: 1; } }
      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .stack-card { animation: none; opacity: 1; } }

      .visit-block { flex: 1 1 280px; max-width: 340px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; }
      .visit-note { display: block; width: 300px; max-width: 100%; height: auto; opacity: 0.8; margin: 0 0 0.9rem 0.5rem; pointer-events: none; }
      .omnibox { position: relative; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 12px 18px; background: #f1f3f4; border: 1px solid #e4e6e8; border-radius: 999px; text-decoration: none; overflow: hidden; transition: background 0.25s ease, box-shadow 0.3s ease, transform 0.25s ease; }
      .omnibox:hover { background: #eceef0; box-shadow: 0 8px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.08); transform: translateY(-1px); }
      .omnibox-lock { width: 13px; height: 13px; color: #5f6368; flex-shrink: 0; }
      .omnibox-url { flex: 1; font-family: 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 0.85rem; color: #202124; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
      .omnibox-arrow { width: 16px; height: 16px; color: #5f6368; flex-shrink: 0; transition: transform 0.25s ease, color 0.25s ease; }
      .omnibox:hover .omnibox-arrow { transform: translateX(4px); color: #202124; }
      .omnibox::after { content: ''; position: absolute; top: 0; left: -60%; width: 55%; height: 100%; background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, rgba(255,255,255,0.75), transparent); transform: skewX(-20deg); pointer-events: none; }
      .omnibox:hover::after { animation: omnibox-shimmer 0.9s ease; }
      @keyframes omnibox-shimmer { from { left: -60%; } to { left: 130%; } }

      /* ——— next project ——— */
      .next-panel { min-height: 70vh; }
      .next { display: inline-flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem; text-decoration: none; }
      .next-kicker { font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); }
      .next-title { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.4rem); font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: -0.012em; color: var(--fg); transition: transform 0.5s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1); }
      .next:hover .next-title { transform: translateX(0.6rem); }

      /* ——— corner chrome (matches /work) ——— */
      .chrome { position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 4; pointer-events: none; mix-blend-mode: difference; }
      .label { position: fixed; font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #fff; }
      .grow { pointer-events: auto; text-decoration: none; white-space: nowrap; line-height: 1; will-change: font-size; transition: font-size 0.62s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1), letter-spacing 0.62s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1), font-weight 0.62s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1); }
      .grow:hover { font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
      .work:hover { font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 5.6rem); }
      .info:hover { font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 3.9rem); }
      html.pre-tl .grow { transition: none; }
      html.pre-tl .work { font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 5.6rem); font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
      .tl { top: 1.9rem; left: 2.2rem; }
      .tr { top: 1.9rem; right: 2.2rem; }
      /* First-paint mobile theme (html.is-mobile set by the head script): kill the desktop
         red text + textured background on the very first frame, before the @media rules
         resolve — this is what removes the flash on navigation. */
      html.is-mobile { --fg: #141414; }
      html.is-mobile, html.is-mobile body { background: #fff; }

      /* ——— Mobile: white/black StudioSmall retheme + natural stacked scroll ———
         Desktop keeps red-on-painterly; on a phone that reads busy, so mobile goes
         plain: white ground, black ink, demos near full-width, and beats stacked
         naturally instead of one-screen-per-beat (which leaves big gaps on a phone). */
      @media (max-width: 768px) {
        :root { --fg: #141414; --ink: #1a1a1a; --muted: rgba(20, 20, 20, 0.46); }
        html { background: #fff; }
        body { background: #fff; overflow-x: hidden; }

        .page { max-width: 100%; margin: 0; padding: 0 1rem; }

        /* beats stack naturally rather than filling a screen each */
        .panel { min-height: auto; padding: 4.5vh 0; }
        .hero-panel { min-height: 74vh; padding-top: 20vh; }
        .next-panel { min-height: auto; padding: 6vh 0 12vh; }

        /* project title a notch below the desktop hero size; kicker softened */
        .title, .subtitle { font-size: clamp(2rem, 8.5vw, 2.5rem); }
        .kicker { color: var(--muted); }
        .scroll-hint { margin-top: 2.4rem; }

        /* demos/screengrabs near full-width */
        .media { max-width: 100%; }

        /* closing: reference deck stacks above the visit link */
        .closing-row { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: 2rem; }
        .stack { width: min(78vw, 320px); }
      }
      /* Touch devices have no hover, so the nav enlarge — both the :hover growth and
         the persisted cross-page handoff (pre-tl/pre-tr) — only reads as a broken
         giant word. Keep the nav labels small and static on mobile. */
      @media (hover: none) {
        .grow, .grow:hover, html.pre-tl .grow, html.pre-tr .grow {
          font-size: 0.72rem !important;
          font-weight: 600 !important;
          letter-spacing: 0.16em !important;
        }
      }

    </style>

    <script>
      window.addEventListener('pointermove', () => {
        document.documentElement.classList.remove('pre-tl');
      }, { once: true });

      // ——— smooth exit: gentle opacity dip, then navigate (internal links only) ———
      const page = document.querySelector('.page');
      const reduceMotion = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
      document.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
        const a = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('a');
        if (!a) return;
        const href = a.getAttribute('href');
        if (!href || a.target === '_blank' || a.hasAttribute('download')) return;
        if (e.metaKey || e.ctrlKey || e.shiftKey || e.altKey || (e as MouseEvent).button !== 0) return;
        const url = new URL(href, location.href);
        if (url.origin !== location.origin || url.pathname === location.pathname) return;
        e.preventDefault();
        if (a.classList.contains('work')) sessionStorage.setItem('navTL', '1');
        if (a.classList.contains('info')) sessionStorage.setItem('navTR', '1');
        if (reduceMotion) { window.location.href = url.href; return; }
        page?.classList.add('leaving');
        setTimeout(() => { window.location.href = url.href; }, 200);
      });
      window.addEventListener('pageshow', (e) => { if (e.persisted) page?.classList.remove('leaving'); });

      // ——— reveal-on-scroll ———
      const reveals = document.querySelectorAll('.reveal');
      if (reduceMotion) {
        reveals.forEach((el) => el.classList.add('in'));
      } else {
        const io = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
          entries.forEach((en) => {
            if (en.isIntersecting) { en.target.classList.add('in'); io.unobserve(en.target); }
          });
        }, { threshold: 0.2, rootMargin: '0px 0px -12% 0px' });
        reveals.forEach((el) => io.observe(el));
      }

      // ——— Vimeo demos: muted, play only while in view, booted lazily ———
      function initVimeoDemos() {
        const iframes = document.querySelectorAll('.vimeo-wrapper iframe');
        if (!iframes.length) return;
        const attach = () => {
          const players = new WeakMap();
          // create each player only when its demo first scrolls into view, so we never
          // boot all of them at once (simultaneous handshakes can trip "Player error")
          const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
            entries.forEach((entry) => {
              const iframe = entry.target as HTMLIFrameElement;
              if (entry.isIntersecting) {
                let player = players.get(iframe);
                if (!player) {
                  player = new (window as any).Vimeo.Player(iframe);
                  player.setVolume(0);
                  players.set(iframe, player);
                }
                player.ready().then(() => player.setVolume(0)).then(() => player.play()).catch(() => {});
              } else {
                const player = players.get(iframe);
                if (player) player.pause().then(() => player.setCurrentTime(0)).catch(() => {});
              }
            });
          }, { threshold: 0.5 });
          iframes.forEach((iframe) => observer.observe(iframe));
        };
        if ((window as any).Vimeo && (window as any).Vimeo.Player) {
          attach();
        } else {
          let api = document.getElementById('vimeo-api') as HTMLScriptElement | null;
          if (!api) {
            api = document.createElement('script');
            api.id = 'vimeo-api';
            api.src = 'https://player.vimeo.com/api/player.js';
            document.head.appendChild(api);
          }
          api.addEventListener('load', attach, { once: true });
        }
      }
      requestAnimationFrame(() => initVimeoDemos());
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
